{
  "title": "What Is a Function? — Reusable Recipes",
  "subtitle": "Defining Functions with def, Parameters & Return Values",
  "topic": "6.1 • WHAT IS A FUNCTION?",
  "body": "<div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px; width: 100%;\">\n  <div style=\"text-align: center; margin-bottom: 4px; width: 100%;\">\n    <div style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 4px 4px 0px #111111; padding: 4px 14px; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: 900; font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px;\">\n      6.1 • Reusable Code Blocks\n    </div>\n    <h1 style=\"font-family: 'Title', 'Body', sans-serif; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 8px 0; text-transform: uppercase;\">\n      Defining <hlt>Functions</hlt> in Python\n    </h1>\n    <p style=\"font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; color: #222222; margin: 0 auto; max-width: 640px;\">\n      A function is a named block of code that performs a specific task. You write the recipe once with <code>def</code>, and run it whenever you call its name!\n    </p>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"lesson-ref-card\">\n    <div class=\"lesson-ref-header\">\n      <span class=\"ref-badge\">PREVIOUS KNOWLEDGE</span>\n      <span class=\"lesson-ref-title\">Connecting to Earlier Concepts</span>\n    </div>\n    <p class=\"lesson-ref-desc\">\n      We've been using built-in functions like print() and range() from Day 1. Now you will build your very own custom functions!\n    </p>\n    <div style=\"display: flex; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap;\">\n      <a href=\"1.html?spcl=1&lsn=2&sub=3&ref_from=1_7_1\" class=\"ref-jump-btn\">Review: Built-in print() Function (Lesson 2.2) →</a>\n      <a href=\"1.html?spcl=1&lsn=3&sub=1&ref_from=1_7_1\" class=\"ref-jump-btn\">Review: Variables as Parameters (Lesson 3.1) →</a>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"background: #fde047; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 6px 6px 0px #111111; border-radius: 4px; padding: 20px;\">\n    <span style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; color: #111111; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #111111; padding: 2px 8px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 900; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 8px;\">\n      Function Anatomy\n    </span>\n    <h2 style=\"font-family: 'Title', 'Body', sans-serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 10px 0; text-transform: uppercase;\">\n      The def & return Keywords\n    </h2>\n    <div style=\"background: #0d1117; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 #111111; padding: 12px 14px; font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; color: #f0f6fc; font-size: 14px; border-radius: 4px;\">\n      <span style=\"color: #ff7b72;\">def</span> <span style=\"color: #d2a8ff;\">add_numbers</span>(a, b):<br/>\n      &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;result = a + b<br/>\n      &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style=\"color: #ff7b72;\">return</span> result<br/><br/>\n      <span style=\"color: #8b949e;\"># Calling the function:</span><br/>\n      answer = add_numbers(<span style=\"color: #7ee787;\">10</span>, <span style=\"color: #7ee787;\">20</span>)<br/>\n      <span style=\"color: #79c0ff;\">print</span>(answer)  <span style=\"color: #8b949e;\"># Outputs: 30</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>"
}